WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:03.790
- [Host] They create worlds from thin air.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.113
They tell stories in silence.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.150
I'm talking, of course, about mimes.

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:13.330
And the many considered
the most famous mime

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.040
in history was not only a
world-renowned performer,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.633
but also saved children from
the Nazis during World War II.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.593
That man was Marcel Marceau.

00:00:28.505 --> 00:00:29.900
- [Shawn] Marcel Marceau is probably

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.270
the most iconic image of mime.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.510
- [Host] And that's Shawn Wen.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:35.343
- [Shawn] Hi.

00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:37.290
- [Host] She's the author
of "A Twenty Minute Silence

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.600
Followed by Applause," a
book about Marceau's life.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.770
- [Shawn] The way that we picture a mime

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.930
is someone who performs without speaking,

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:48.720
and a lot of this has to
do with Marcel Marceau.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.940
He really influenced a
lot of our visual culture.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.240
Michael Jackson's moonwalk is modeled

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.130
after his walking against the wind.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:01.010
He performed up until his death in 2007,

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.963
and he toured the world
over and over again.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.930
- [Host] Before his legacy as a mime,

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.113
Marceau was a young boy in France.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:13.390
It was here he would find
his hero in the movies.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:16.070
- [Shawn] His inspiration
was Charlie Chaplin,

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:19.070
his humor, his use of physicality.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.690
Even from a young age,
Mareau displayed this

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.333
kind of like uncanny physical gift.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.789
- [Host] However, in May
of 1940, Marceau's life

00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:30.510
would change forever.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.270
- [Shawn] Marceau was 16 years old

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:35.840
when Germany marched on
France and his childhood

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.910
ended all at once.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.530
Marceau's father died in Auschwitz,

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.950
and both he and his brother
were very much involved

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.923
in the war effort against the Nazis.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.120
- [Host] And it was Marceau's skills

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.593
as a performer that
made him a unique asset.

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:53.352
- [Shawn] There's a story
about Marcel Marceau

00:01:53.352 --> 00:01:57.220
saving a group of children
from an orphanage.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.610
He dressed them up as campers,

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:02.040
and he would walk them
into safety in Switzerland.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.690
He was doing mimicry, and he was acting,

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.493
and, essentially, he was entertaining them

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:09.340
to the point where they could pretend

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.230
as if they were going on vacation,

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.393
rather than fleeing for their lives.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:20.220
Another story was that he was encountering

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.563
a large group of 30 German soldiers.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.980
And in that moment, he
pretended that he was actually

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:32.700
at the front of a large
group of French soldiers,

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.410
and they actually surrendered to him.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:40.051
It seems as if this
natural knack for acting

00:02:40.051 --> 00:02:43.340
ended up becoming a
part of his involvement

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:44.373
in the war effort.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.330
It's been described that
he wasn't just miming

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:49.040
because he loved mime.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.343
During the war he was miming for his life.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.450
- [Host] In many ways,
Marceau's wartime experience

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.600
would shape his life's work.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:03.220
- [Shawn] He spent his
life circling the world

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.107
over and over again, telling these stories

00:03:06.107 --> 00:03:10.623
through his body in a
way that defied language.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:13.050
There's something about that

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.570
that almost seems like an effort

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.540
to bring the world back together

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:20.730
doing something that anyone,
regardless of language

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.290
or nationality, can understand

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.703
just by looking at him.

00:03:26.144 --> 00:03:28.811
(serious music)

